# R3f: Z1 12-key keypad from vendor kernel reverse engineering.
# Mainline driver registers as "mt6779-keypad".
# Numbers below are Linux EV_KEY codes, not MSC_SCAN matrix values.
# Requested: 复读(repeat) = VOLUME_DOWN, 跟读(follow) = VOLUME_UP.
# Existing 250/251/252/254 assignments are unverified physical-key candidates.
# Preserve these assignments until labeled getevent captures identify the keys.
# Android 9 rejects the legacy WAKE and WAKE_DROPPED flags.
key 114   VOLUME_DOWN
key 251   VOLUME_DOWN
key 250   VOLUME_UP
key 115   VOLUME_UP
key 252   VOLUME_UP
key 106   DPAD_RIGHT
key 232   DPAD_CENTER
key 105   DPAD_LEFT
key 103   DPAD_UP
key 158   BACK
key 108   DPAD_DOWN
key 254   VOLUME_DOWN
